            <ArticleTitle>Lateral patellar chamfer in total knee arthroplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>713-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Derangement of the anterior compartment of the knee can cause patellofemoral dysfunction in up to 50% of secondary surgeries after total knee arthroplasty. A technique of patellar chamfering is described that can minimize the risk of anterior knee pain from lateral patellar impingement without compromising bone stock for future operations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
